# The vendored packages are verbatim copies of the upstream tarballs, and the
# sha256 values in PINS.md are of those tarballs. With core.autocrlf=input
# (common on this team's machines) git would rewrite the CRLF line endings in
# the packages' Schematron files on the way into the index, and a fresh clone
# would then no longer byte-match what was pinned. Turn all normalisation off
# for the vendored trees so the claim in PINS.md and README.md stays true.
packages/** -text
dist/*.tgz binary
